  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124445,
      "id": "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340",
      "title": "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6b68d726-5fd5-5aea-989e-6abf43f6a5f3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $g(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4x-4y-4z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇g(x,y,z)=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4x-4y-4z) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+0+0-4-0-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1-4 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4x-4y-4z) \\\\  & =0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+0-0-4-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1-4 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4x-4y-4z) \\\\  & =0+0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+z\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}-0-0-4 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1-4 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)\\,i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-3)\\,j+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-3)\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)\\,i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-3)\\,j+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-3)\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y-3=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z-3=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=e^{3}.$  Similarly, from the second and third equations, we obtain $y=e^{3}$ and $z=e^{3}.$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=0$ at the point $(e^{3},e^{3},e^{3}).$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7b8632bf-b74b-5d5e-99c4-5de33d222d03",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
