    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b03b6c2f-d156-520c-8488-b6843493ebd3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{48}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{8}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{48}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{8}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{8}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{48z+8y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{48}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{8}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{48+6x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{48}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{8}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{8}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{48z+8y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{48+6x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{8+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{48z+8y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{48+6x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{8+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{48z+8y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{48+6x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{8+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-8.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{8+{z}^{2}(-8)}{{z}^{2}(-8)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-8$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{48z+8y}{(-8)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ 48z+8y & =0 \\\\ y & =-6z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-6$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=6.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-8,-6,1)$ and $(-8,6,-1).$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
