      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{4}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{2}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{2}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{2}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4z+2y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{4}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{2}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4+2x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{4}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{2}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{2}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{4z+2y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{4+2x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{2+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4z+2y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{4+2x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{2+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4z+2y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{4+2x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{2+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-2.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{2+{z}^{2}(-2)}{{z}^{2}(-2)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4z+2y}{(-2)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ 4z+2y & =0 \\\\ y & =-2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-2$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=2.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-2,-2,1)$ and $(-2,2,-1).$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b5808744-9eab-5027-a82a-6ac4950b0aa0",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
