    "question": {
      ":question/id": "97db714f-44c0-5138-9f96-c0045771fa9a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{30}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{5}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{30}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{5}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{30}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{5}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{30z+5y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{30}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{5}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{30}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{30+6x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{30}{xy}+\\frac{6}{y}+\\frac{5}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{5}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{30z+5y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{30+6x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{5+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{30z+5y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{30+6x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{5+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{30z+5y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{30+6x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{5+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-5.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{5+{z}^{2}(-5)}{{z}^{2}(-5)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-5$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{30z+5y}{(-5)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ 30z+5y & =0 \\\\ y & =-6z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-6$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=6.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-5,-6,1)$ and $(-5,6,-1).$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
